ately quickly to ruin the narrative-climatic liquidity very main character started …. Because Max has mentality of the thug devoid of values standing out from the crowd of other brawlers with exclusively an Australian accent. Upgrading one's cart is an only purpose motivating him - I was under the impression that for gaining access to the new bumper he would be able vacantly to shoot the pregnant woman dead (in accordance with the principle: "and need it - and of it get it"). His actions are lacking sensible motivation - wants only to kill and to destroy more in order can go more quickly. Surprisingly - quite not better the case looks in case of marginal heroes. The entire gallery of figures having a potential constitutes the blend of rolls of film noninteresting, deprived of the personality and character, can except for a little bit of unstable Chumbucketa - of the personal Maxa mechanic and the designer of his quad bike (of called solemnly Magnum Opus). I don't know, whether behind such a state of affairs I should not burden the plot which it is possible to summarize with the fault with words: Max after loss of the first car wants to get the second car, avenging himself by the way too first. And so he is collecting the rustheap and is smashing the half of Wildernesses in order to get one's hands on the V8 engine. That kind of history won't leave too much space for ambition, but all games turning up at the more late part, "more serious" subplots, trying at least symbolically uplastycznić story, I shrugged off - because I knew that for Maxa they weren't outweighing.
Pluses: the splendid climate, the cohesion of the represented world and keeping spirits of film originals;
functional and imaginative project of the location;
give the mechanic and the diversity of skirmishes;
spectacular, sophisticated realization of the sequence jeżdżonych;
enough developed system of improvements of the hero and his cart;
considerable, diverse, well developed world;
the graphical cover and the optimization.
Minuses: the crude, schematic plot and heroes insipid, not-falling into the memory;
repetitiveness of all activities - of both the mission, and optional tasks;
subordinating the entire game to clearing scrap away;
monotony accompanying the games all along the way.

