Just one more ...
I lost track of how many times I would say that while playing Rogue Legacy.  It's pleasing, 16-bit, art style pulled me in on first load.  The simple jump, slash, dodge gameplay gradually changed the longer I played.  It began to evolve and gain more depth with each new character class unlocked, pushing me to try new play styles and further honing my knights agility and strength.  The core action platformer gameplay is as solid and, honestly, flawless.  The further you go and the more you play the difficulty will build and build and you will die over and over and over again but never feel cheated.  Every room cleared gives a sense of reward and satisfaction and each boss slain is hard earned and worth every knight sacrificed until you become powerful enough to stand up to them.  Each hour gives a constant progression of ability, character, wealth and sacrifice that will leave you saying;
Just one more...

in a word, this game has a great idea--hunting in wild areas. But at the beginning, there were so many bugs:
i had killed one prey, there were some still hanging around like nothing had happened;
maybe because of the model of the map, more often than sometimes, a prey could been stucked among stones or sth, you could do it with a knife if you had;
i had killed one, other preys have been scared, then they just runned around not away.
the 3 bugs mentioned above appeared in the lake reserve(the 2nd) on my laptop.
after installing patch 1.1, the frame number becomes higher, and i haven't found any one of the bugs appeared yet. so the experience is more comfortable. but harder to get to harvest...

